   "id": "gittin.62a.12",
   "daf": "62a",
   "sentenceId": 11,
   "he": "וְאֵין כּוֹפְלִין ״שָׁלוֹם״ לְגוֹי: רַב חִסְדָּא מַקְדֵּים וְיָהֵיב לְהוּ שְׁלָמָא. רַב כָּהֲנָא אֲמַר לְהוּ ״שְׁלָמָא לְמָר״.",
   "en": "It was stated above in the name of Rav that «one may not double the greeting» of shalom extended «to a gentile.» The Gemara relates that «Rav Ḥisda» would «greet» gentiles «first» so that he would not have to respond to the greeting extended to him with a twofold shalom. «Rav Kahana,» by contrast, would wait for their greeting, and then «say to them: Peace to my master,» thereby freeing himself from having to say shalom twice."
  }
 ],
